selective client loading
	for the following discussion "load a node" means to send the node and all children of that node, owned or not, to the client.
		This definition is not recursive.  Children of children are not included in this definition.  Although it is common that loading is executed recursively.
		Loaded is a state of the node in the graph in memory.  Graph in database doesn't have this state.
			An unloaded node has no children in-graph.  
			A loaded node may or may not have children.
		Client user interface will show unloaded nodes differently.  Hollow circle for the fold.
		Client graph may be different from Server graph.  This requirement does not introduce unloaded server nodes.  It does introduce unloaded client nodes.
		When an unloaded node becomes loaded, its state becomes the database state.
	when client starts, load the root workspace.
		recursively load every node that is transitively owned by the workspace. But do not load other workspaces.
		Prior to this changeset all server nodes always came to client.  This changeset makes that no longer automatic, but the Load command will make it happen.
	The Upload command is extended and renamed to simply Load.  
		currently used for 
			Load file data from client (desktop app) filespace to server filespace
			Load file data in server into server nodes
		Newly will also send server nodes to client, if the client doesn't already have them.
			Load all children transitively owned by that node, but not other workspaces.
			This is the third action of a sequence.  In some cases the others don't apply and only this needs to be done.
	Graph nav
		If the user operation (eg. zoom; unfold) demands children of graph node that is not loaded, we fail it
		search dialog does not load unloaded nodes.  
			Search algorithm doesn't delve into children of unloaded nodes
			If an unloaded node is chosen as the search target, 
				we load it recursively.
			if an unloaded node is chosen as a move target
				we load exactly that node.
				and then execute move.
	Graph edits
		edits that happen on the client keep client nodes loaded
		The server can send graph changes.  Those changes can now involve parent nodes not in the graph.  We need to reconcile our nodeset
			Operations on a single node
				If we have the node, we can change it
				otherwise ignore it
			Add node
				accept op
			Add child to parent / Remove child from parent
				Allow if we have parent and child
				and parent is set to loaded.
	
